  "comments": "<p>First released into circulation, in individual Brilliant Uncirculated Royal Mint pack and as part of the Annual Coin Sets for 1994, in both Brilliant Uncirculated &amp; Proof versions, the design was also struck in silver proof, silver piedfort and gold proof.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5ed005d179991.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5ed005d179991.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/603112bdb90b6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/603112bdb90b6.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>The design was reissued in copper-nickel in 2009 with Ian Rank Broadley's fourth portrait in the 16-piece sets to commemorate the 40th anniversary of the 50 pence denomination, then again in 2019 with Jody Clark's fifth portrait, forming part of the 5-coin British Military set celebrating 50 years of the 50p.<br><br>The reverse designer's initials are located below the denomination.</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/66938d36f1d9b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/66938d36f1d9b.jpg\"></a></p>",
